From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:27:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): dismiss items from the open-items bar

An open item the agent will not get back to soon still takes a chip in the
open-items bar on every visit. Each open row in the expanded list now has a
dismiss control; a dismissed item leaves the header chips and the open
count, and a "Show dismissed (N)" toggle at the bottom lists it with a
Restore button so the dismissal is reversible. An item the agent later
closes shows as closed as usual.

The dismissed labels are stored on the session itself, as the
`omnigent.items_dismissed` label (a comma list, oldest forgotten if it
would outgrow the label column) through the existing session-label write
(`PATCH /v1/sessions/{id}`), so the state follows the user across devices
rather than living in one browser. The Omnigent-namespaced key is one the
server lets clients set and the label editor hides. A write in flight is
read as the current value so a dismiss takes effect at once.

Local only: this extends the chat-item-labels series (the open-items
tracker), which is not upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
